# Pairs with EveryAckedWriteMaterialised. A leaf stop costs nothing from the
# fault budget, so a leaf may be torn down before it reads its own write on
# every activation for ever. This perturbs the ENVIRONMENT assumption that
# faults do not recur for ever, not the protocol: it shows the property needs
# that assumption, and is not one of the protocol-defect liveness pairings
# (those are ReadPositionTracksOwnEntries, ResidualAdvanceNeverPersisted and
# SwitchKeepsFence).
MODULE: EveryAckedWriteMaterialisedLeafStopsUnbounded
TARGET: EveryAckedWriteMaterialised
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: leaf stops are not bounded, so a leaf can be restarted before every read for ever
PERTURBS: LeafStop

--- FIND
    /\ cov' = [cov EXCEPT ![l] = NoSnap]
    /\ faults' = faults + 1
--- REPLACE
    /\ cov' = [cov EXCEPT ![l] = NoSnap]
\* MUTATION: the stop does not spend the fault budget.
    /\ faults' = faults
--- END